Protocol is AGENTS.md.

This repo lives on the experimental contract runtime under `.artifacts/`.
At session start, if views were not injected, run
`adaptive-artifacts hook-start` and read the derived
views (also under `.artifacts/views/` after a start hook). Capture records
at the event with `adaptive-artifacts` (`create`, `supersede`, `update`,
`correct`, `contradict`, `capture`). Views are derived — regenerate, do
not edit. At session end, if facts changed write records, regenerate
views (`handoff --out views/handoff.md`, `view --id
project:investigation-summary --out views/investigation-summary.md`),
and run `hook-stop`. Fix validation errors before finishing.

Do not recreate a separate `.records/` or `adaptive-artifacts/` tree.
Do not amend shipped skills, catalog, runtime, or `hooks/` mid-task.
Extension-change evidence lives in this store and needs human approval.
The skill names are `design-artifacts`, `artifact-runtime`, and
`reassess-artifacts`. This repo uses the installed plugin CLI
(`adaptive-artifacts`), not `./tools/artifacts.py`.

`design/DESIGN.md` is experimental design rationale, not the live
protocol and not a store authority.
